#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate the sample fabric-spec dataset for the Indus Weaves search tool.

Run:      python generate_data.py
Output:   data/fabric_specs.json   (a JSON list, one object per fabric)

Needs only Python 3.8+. No packages to install. The output is identical every time
you run it (no randomness), so the JSON file can be committed to git.

IMPORTANT: this is SYNTHETIC sample data. The numbers look realistic but are not lab
results and are not real Indus Weaves specifications. Do not use them for real orders.

How it works
  1. FABRICS (below) is the hand-written table of 27 fabrics: the raw facts.
  2. build_entry() turns each row into a full entry: it adds the unique ID, the
     composition text ("65% Polyester, 35% Cotton"), the category, the source name,
     and one plain-English `text` snippet that the search tool will read later.
  3. validate() checks the result (20-30 entries, unique IDs and names,
     percentages add up to 100, nothing empty) and refuses to save bad data.

To add a fabric: copy one block in FABRICS, edit it, run the script again.
"""
